	Running S3-ST200.PRG
	====================

	Check that your master disk is write-protected (tab open).

	S3-ST can be installed on a double-sided floppy disk or on a 
	hard disk partition. It requires approximately 450 Kbytes of 
	disk space. Installation on a floppy disk is probably best; 
	many of the files will only be needed once; you can copy the 
	main program files onto a hard disk later if you wish. 

	Double-click on S3-ST200.PRG on the master disk. The program 
	will display a GEM dialogue. Type in the letter of the drive on 
	which S3-ST should be installed. (On single drive systems, you 
	can change disks at this point.) Then click on "OK" or press the 
	Return key. The program will display names of files as they are 
	created.
	_________________________________________________________________

	All the files are written in a folder named S3-ST2.00, and 
	are arranged as follows:

	S3-ST.PRG  }		The main program 
	S3-ST.HLQ  }		and its help
	S3-ST.RSC  }		and resource files

	MANUAL\
	      MANUAL.PRG  }	Program to print the manuals
	      MANUAL.RSC  }	and its resource file

	      README.TXT	Introduction to S3-ST
	      WHATSNEW.TXT	Summary of new features in version 2
	      MANUAL.TXT	The main manual

	      REGISTER.TXT	To register for news of updates and to
				have your say on future development
	      BUGREPRT.TXT	For your bug reports

	SERIAL.BUG\		Patches for TOS RS232 bugs

	SERIES.3\
	      INSTALL.PRG }	Program to install server software 
	      INSTALL.RSC }	on Series 3, and its resource and
	      INSTALL.TXT }	data files
	      ST-COMM1.OPA	Series 3 server program
	      ST-COMM2.OPA	Series 3a server program
	      ST-I.OPL		Temporary Series 3 program
				used by install.prg
	VIEWERS\
	      DBFVIEW.ACC	Accessory and Program versions of a
	      DBFVIEW.PRG	program to view, and copy from, Psion
				Database (e.g. address) files on Ataris
	      DBFVIEW.SET	Text file mapping Psion to Atari 
				character sets.
	      CHARSET.DBF	Example DBF file listing the Psion
				character set.

	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	Print the manual by running MANUAL\MANUAL.PRG. This will print in
	either single or double-sided format, and adds page numbers. The
	manual is in three parts and the program lets you choose which to
	print. As a minimum, you should read the Introduction, README.TXT.
	You can also print or view the manual files from the GEM desktop.
	~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
